  "body": "## What changed\n`xtask/src/scan.rs` `test_fns` ended each test span by counting every `{`/`}`, including those inside string literals, so `refuse(\"{\", \"bad JSON\")` in `fixture_library.rs` swallowed the next test and `cargo xtask gate test <next test>` reported \"no #[test] fn matches\".\n\nThe depth count now goes through the new `xtask/src/braces.rs`, which skips braces inside `\"...\"` (with `\\\\` and `\\\"` escapes), raw strings (`r\"...\"`, `r#\"...\"#`, any number of `#`), char literals (`'{'`, `'\\''`, `'\\u{7d}'`; lifetimes like `'a` are left alone) and `//` comments. The lexer state carries across lines, so multi-line strings work. No unwrap/expect/panic.\n\nThe quick tier's changed-fn picker uses the same `test_fns` spans, so it is fixed by the same change.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 30 passed (3 new), `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n- Pinning tests: `braces_in_string_literals_do_not_swallow_the_next_test`, `braces_in_raw_strings_chars_comments_and_lifetimes_are_ignored`, `a_change_in_the_test_after_a_brace_string_is_attributed_to_it` (quick planner: a hunk in the second test plans `--exact second`).\n- Repro commands from the issue, with `--dry-run`: `the_library_folder_is_the_override_else_a_sibling_of_machines` before: \"no #[test] fn matches\"; after: `app fixture_library  dry run`. `a_bad_library_is_refused_whole_by_name` finds its test as before.\n\n## Not exercised\nBlock comments (`/* { */`) are not skipped (not in the issue's scope). Full batch/release tiers not run (tooling only).\n\n## Process\n`xtask/` is a process file: `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` bumped 10 -> 11. A fork must do nothing beyond the normal process sync. Fork synced at v0.16.0.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #764\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
